Use Three.js to implement a shoe AR virtual try-on simulator. Load a shoe model and align it with a foot placeholder, with support for size scaling, left/right foot switching, fine angle adjustment, and snapshots.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/MaterialsVariantsShoe.glb;
(2) After loading is complete, center the shoe model and scale it appropriately;
(3) After loading is complete, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[Foot Placeholder]
(4) Create a foot placeholder: use a BoxGeometry cuboid with width 0.3, height 0.15, and length 0.8, with a semi-transparent skin-colored material (0xffd1a4, opacity 0.5), to simulate the shape and position of a foot;
(5) Place the foot above a platform consisting of a gray circular CylinderGeometry;

[Shoe Alignment]
(6) Automatically align the shoe above the foot placeholder, with its position and rotation adjusted so that it looks as though it is being worn on the foot;

[Size Controls]
(7) Add a size slider (id="sizeSlider", range 36-46, step 1, default 40) corresponding to European shoe sizes;
(8) When the slider changes, scale the shoe model proportionally: use size 40 as the baseline (scale=1.0), and scale by ±3% for each one-size increase or decrease;
(9) Scale the foot placeholder synchronously as well;
(10) Display the current size beside it (id="sizeDisplay");

[Left/Right Foot Switching]
(11) Add a toggle button (id="footToggle") that switches between "Left Foot" and "Right Foot";
(12) When switching, mirror the shoe model along the X axis (scale.x *= -1), and mirror the foot placeholder correspondingly;
(13) Update window.__3D_STATE__.footSide ('left' or 'right');

[Fine Angle Adjustment]
(14) Add a rotation slider (id="rotationSlider", range -15 to +15, step 1, default 0), in degrees;
(15) Control the shoe's fine rotation angle around the Y axis (vertical axis);

[Snapshot Functionality]
(16) Add a "Snapshot" button (id="snapshotBtn");
(17) When clicked, use renderer.domElement.toDataURL() to capture the current view;
(18) Add the thumbnail to the snapshot gallery area below the page (id="snapshotGallery");
(19) For each snapshot, increment window.__3D_STATE__.snapshotCount++;

[OrbitControls]
(20) Use OrbitControls to enable orbiting around the shoe and viewing it from all angles;

[HUD Display]
(21) The HUD panel in the upper-left corner must display:
  - Current size (id="currentSize", for example, "EU 40");
  - Foot side (id="footSideDisplay", "Left Foot" / "Right Foot");
  - Rotation angle (id="rotationDisplay");
  - Snapshot count (id="snapshotCountDisplay");
  - Model loading status (id="loadStatus");

[Visual Effects]
(22) Use a light gray gradient (0xf0f0f0) for the scene background;
(23) Add 3-point lighting: Key light + Fill light + Rim light;
(24) Add a circular shadow beneath the platform (shadow plane);

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean (whether model loading is complete)
  - currentSize: number (current European size 36-46)
  - footSide: string ('left' or 'right')
  - rotationAngle: number (rotation angle -15 to 15)
  - snapshotCount: number (number of snapshots)
  - shoeScale: number (current shoe scale factor)
  - cameraDistance: number (camera distance)

Output a single standalone HTML file. Place this file in the same directory as the assets/ folder and run it through a local HTTP server.
